A banner above a procedure closed C-style: the comment runs on to the
first `;`, which ends the :PROCEDURE line, so the declaration is inside
the comment. comment_swallows_code (warning) names the swallowed
fragment; the orphaned :ENDPROC then surfaces as unmatched_block_end,
the puzzling symptom the catalog rationale describes
(diag.comment_swallows_code).
Suspected issue: the range of a diagnostic on a multi-line comment ends on the comment's first line at column start+token length (past the line's end) instead of at the comment's real end; diag.c_style_comment_closer says "The range covers the comment."
-- input.ssl --
/* Helper: trims and upper-cases a code
*/
:PROCEDURE CleanCode;
	:PARAMETERS sCode;
	:RETURN Upper(AllTrim(sCode));
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
/* Helper: trims and upper-cases a code
*/
:PROCEDURE CleanCode;
:PARAMETERS sCode;
:RETURN Upper(AllTrim(sCode));
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
1:1-1:65 warning comment_swallows_code: This comment does not end at its '*/' - SSL comments end at ';', so it runs on and swallows ':PROCEDURE CleanCode'. That code never executes. End the comment with ';'
6:1-6:9 error unmatched_block_end: Unexpected ':ENDPROC' without matching block start
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
1:1-1:65 warning comment_swallows_code: This comment does not end at its '*/' - SSL comments end at ';', so it runs on and swallows ':PROCEDURE CleanCode'. That code never executes. End the comment with ';'
6:1-6:9 error unmatched_block_end: Unexpected ':ENDPROC' without matching block start
